<title>SWEDEN: Volvo U.S. car sales dip 0.8 pct in Aug.</title>
<headline>Volvo U.S. car sales dip 0.8 pct in Aug.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish vehicle manufacturer AB Volvo on Tuesday said sales of its cars in the U.S. fell 0.8 percent in August to 7,288.  </p>
<p>For the year to August, Volvo's car sales in the U.S. have fallen by one percent to 62,233.</p>
<p>In Canada, Volvo sold 5,385 cars for the eight months ending August which was a 0.7 percent fall from a year ago.</p>
<p>Volvo said sales of the Volvo 850 and Volvo 960 series in the U.S. were developing strongly with an increase of 13 percent and 23 percent respectively in August compared to August in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
